# Python dependencies for the document tools (issue #24).
#
# This file records intent; requirements.lock and requirements-dev.lock carry
# the exact pins. Everything is pinned with `==` and installed with
# `--no-deps`, so the closure must be complete.
#
# markitdown is the Microsoft converter and the owner-required reader. Only the
# four format extras are requested: `all` would also pull audio/video
# transcription and Azure cloud clients. XLSX brings pandas, DOCX brings lxml;
# both are native packages and therefore live in requirements-dev.lock (and in
# apk-packages.txt for the image).
#
# Native packages (onnxruntime, numpy, pandas, lxml, openpyxl, cryptography,
# pillow) are Alpine packages in the image and PyPI wheels in the development
# virtualenv. pandoc is absent: a ~150 MB binary with no consumer here.
markitdown[docx,xlsx,pptx,pdf]==0.1.9
python-docx==1.2.0
openpyxl==3.1.5
reportlab==5.1.0
pillow==12.2.0
